+/*
+ * x45btsrc.c - the Bluetooth output of the X45: A2DP source + AVRCP target, headless.
+ * Derived from a2dp_source_demo.c and gap_inquiry.c. The panel software starts it (through x45btout-run),
+ * talks to it with lines on stdin and reads its answer from a status file:
+ *
+ *   commands (one per line)          scan | stopscan | connect ADDR | disconnect | forget ADDR | auto ADDR|none
+ *   status file (key=value lines)    /tmp/x45btout.status, rewritten atomically on every change
+ *   audio                            raw PCM, 44100 Hz, 16 bit, stereo, little endian, read from a FIFO that
+ *                                    MPD's "bluetooth" output writes (X45BTOUT_PCM, default /tmp/x45btout.pcm)
+ *
+ * What it does:
+ *  - scan: an inquiry, then the names of the audio devices that did not send one are asked for;
+ *    the list of what was heard (and of the devices paired earlier) goes into the status file
+ *  - connect: opens the audio link to a device (pairing it first when it is not paired: a headset has no
+ *    display, so the pairing is accepted for the device the owner chose and for no other); the device must
+ *    be in pairing mode for a first connection, a paired one only needs to be switched on
+ *  - auto: the device to call again by itself whenever the link is down (switched off and on again)
+ *  - audio: the PCM from the FIFO is SBC-encoded in real time. The stream starts when sound arrives and is
+ *    suspended again after a pause in it, so a paused player lets the headset go quiet
+ *  - the headset's play/pause/next/previous keys are passed on to MPD
+ */
+
